<%#
  FR-58 — the diagnostics view. *"What failed, the template, the Liquid line where
  applicable, engine and version, duration and a correlation id."*

  --- WHY THIS IS A PANEL AND NOT A DOCUMENT ---

  INV-5, and §7b.3's opening sentence: in the base plugin the exception message IS the PDF
  bytes, so a recipient gets a file named `.pdf` that is not one. Here a failure is an HTML
  panel with an HTTP status on the response and no bytes sent at all.

  --- WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT PRINTED ---

  `Diagnostic#detail` — the raw exception text. §7b.3: the old failure leaked SQL
  fragments, role ids and project ids to whoever the report reached. `Diagnostic#to_h`
  cannot carry it either, so no future serialiser picks it up by accident. It is in the
  application log, where the person who can read a stack trace is.
%>
<div class="flash error" id="reporter-report-diagnostic">
  <p><strong><%= reporter_diagnostic_headline(diagnostic) %></strong></p>
  <p><%= diagnostic.message %></p>
</div>

<table class="list">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <th><%= l(:label_reporter_report_diagnostic_code) %></th>
      <td><%= diagnostic.code %></td>
    </tr>
    <% if diagnostic.line %>
      <tr>
        <th><%= l(:label_reporter_report_diagnostic_line) %></th>
        <td><%= diagnostic.line %></td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
    <% if diagnostic.engine %>
      <tr>
        <th><%= l(:label_reporter_preflight_engine_version) %></th>
        <td><%= diagnostic.engine %> <%= diagnostic.engine_version %></td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
    <% if diagnostic.duration_ms %>
      <tr>
        <th><%= l(:label_reporter_preflight_duration) %></th>
        <td><%= diagnostic.duration_ms %> ms</td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
    <tr>
      <th><%= l(:label_reporter_report_diagnostic_correlation_id) %></th>
      <%# The one value a reader is asked to quote in a bug report, so it is selectable
          text rather than part of a sentence. %>
      <td><code><%= diagnostic.correlation_id %></code></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
